    {
      "limitation_id": "topic:doac-vte-recurrence:riskofbias:randomised-contrast",
      "kind": "RANDOMISED_CONTRAST",
      "limitation_class": "INFORMATIONAL",
      "severity": "QUALIFIES_CLAIM",
      "claim_affected": "randomised intervention contrast",
      "evidence_state": "RECORDED",
      "source_fields": [
        "/arm_contrast/trials"
      ],
      "rendered_text": "<div class='absent'><strong>Randomised-contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the registry arm structure &mdash; disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>6 of 6</strong> pooled trials have a registry-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest differs across arms). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> &mdash; a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>19966341</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>dabigatran etexilate 150 mg; warfarin (inr 2-3)</td></tr><tr><td>21128814</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>enoxaparin followed by vka; rivaroxaban (xarelto, bay59-7939)</td></tr><tr><td>22449293</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>enoxaparin overlapping with and followed by vka; rivaroxaban (xarelto, bay59-7939)</td></tr><tr><td>23808982</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>apixaban; enoxaparin; warfarin</td></tr><tr><td>23991658</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>edoxaban tosylate(du-176b); warfarin</td></tr><tr><td>24344086</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>dabigatran etexilate; warfarin</td></tr></table></div>",
      "text_sha256": "fbbca1a7e1bd9f2dcb8162bfa2a11e6b660c063b035ed020b594b9a6002dc394",
      "linked_decision": {
